WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.199
Hi, I'm Hawser!

00:00:02.199 --> 00:00:04.926
Modular just published the whole Mojo and MAX stack.

00:00:04.926 --> 00:00:06.440
Here is how it works.

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:12.699
The new part is the middle: graph compiler, runtime and plugins.

00:00:12.699 --> 00:00:15.404
You can read and patch them, not fork them.

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.890
The parser skips the syntax tree and writes Mojo straight into an

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.197
MLIR dialect called lit.

00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.667
That lowers to kgen and pop, still generic over things like vector width.

00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:32.472
The elaborator fills in every parameter.

00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:34.857
Here, the width became sixteen lanes.

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:38.633
Then LLVM emits code for the CPU or the GPU.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:43.462
A model enters as RMO, which accepts unknown shapes.

00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:47.414
It lowers to strictly typed MO for shape inference and folding.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.995
In MAP, each op is a loop nest, and elementwise chains

00:00:50.995 --> 00:00:52.145
fuse into their neighbours.

00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:56.155
MOGG then generates code from the Mojo kernel library.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:02.513
Below, the runtime runs the graph, and its driver moves memory and launches kernels.

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:06.244
The driver reaches hardware only through a small C interface.

00:01:06.664 --> 00:01:09.337
Each plugin maps those calls to a vendor driver.

00:01:09.337 --> 00:01:10.228
Four are public.

00:01:12.175 --> 00:01:15.112
Modular's own diagram: the graph compiler in the middle.

00:01:15.532 --> 00:01:17.791
The runtime at the bottom, above the hardware.

00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:22.224
Mojo, its compiler and the kernel library are Apache.

00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:29.251
The new internals allow binaries, services and upstream fixes, but no public forks.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:34.017
A forty line Mojo kernel came close to NumPy on one core.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.200
Readable is not forkable.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.925
Mojo is open source; MAX's core is source you may read and patch upstream.

00:01:46.192 --> 00:01:47.750
Mojo lowers through MLIR.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.087
MAX fuses in its graph compiler.

00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:52.035
Read and contribute, not fork.

00:01:52.455 --> 00:01:54.501
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.085
I'm Hawser.

00:01:55.085 --> 00:01:55.378
Bye!
